      '  object RecordsList: TRecordsListEh'
      '    Data = ('
      '      ('
      '        2'
      '        '
      
        '          '#39'Also known as the big spotted triggerfish.  Inhabits ' +
        'outer reef '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'areas and feeds upon crustaceans and mollusks by crus' +
        'hing them w'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ith powerful teeth.  They are voracious eaters, and d' +
        'ivers repor'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39't seeing the clown triggerfish devour beds of pearl o' +
        'ysters.'#39'#10#10'#39'Do'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' not eat this fish.  According to an 1878 account, "t' +
        'he poisonou'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39's flesh acts primarily upon the nervous tissue of the' +
        ' stomach, o'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ccasioning violent spasms of that organ, and shortly ' +
        'afterwards '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'all the muscles of the body.  The frame becomes rocke' +
        'd with spas'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ms, the tongue thickened, the eye fixed, the breathin' +
        'g laborious'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39', and the patient expires in a paroxysm of extreme su' +
        'ffering."'#39'#10#10 +'
      
        '          '#39'Not edible.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is Indo-Pacific and East Afr' +
        'ica to Somoa.'#39'#10'
      '        {'
      
