      '        '
      
        '          '#39'This is the largest of all the wrasse.  It is found i' +
        'n dense ree'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'f areas, feeding on a wide variety of mollusks, fishe' +
        's, sea urch'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ins, crustaceans, and other invertebrates. In spite o' +
        'f its immen'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'se size, divers find it a very wary fish.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edib' +
        'ility is consider'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ed poor.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is the Indo-Pacific and the Red' +
        ' Sea.'#39'#10'
