        '          '#39'Also know as the grinder ray because of its flat grin' +
        'ding teeth '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'used to crush its meal of crustaceans or invertebrate' +
        's.  Inhabit'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39's bays, sloughs, and kelp beds with sandy bottoms.'#39'#1' +
        '0#10'#39'The bat ray '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'digs up food with its wings and snout, and will even ' +
        'bite off ov'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'erhanging ledges to get at prey.  It hunts singly or ' +
        'in groups. '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' When resting, it buries itself in sand with just the' +
        ' eyes protr'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'uding.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is poor.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is from' +
        ' Oregon to the Gulf of '#39' +'
      '          '#39'California.'#39'#10'
