        '          '#39'This fish hides in a shallow-water lair with just its' +
        ' head protr'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'uding during the day.  At night it feeds on octopuses' +
        ', crustacea'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ns, and small fish close by.'#39'#10#10'#39'If caught, it wil' +
        'l bite anything n'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'earby with its large fang-like teeth.  Divers can be ' +
        'bitten by a'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' moray eel when sticking their hands into crevices or' +
        ' holes in s'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'earch of lobster or abalone.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is good' +
        '.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is from '#39' +'
      '          '#39'Southern California to Southern Baja.'#39
