        '          '#39'Often called the great marbled sculpin.  Found over r' +
        'ocky or she'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'll-encrusted bottoms from shallow to moderately deep ' +
        'waters.  It'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' feeds primarily on crustaceans and mollusks.'#39'#10#10'#39 +
        'The male cabezon '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'will not budge while guarding its nest and can even b' +
        'e touched b'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'y divers.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is good; the flesh is blui' +
        'sh-green but turn'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39's white when cooked.  The eggs of the cabezon are poi' +
        'sonous.'#39'#10#10'#39'Ra'#39' +'
      '          '#39'nge is from Alaska to Central Baja.'#39'#10'
