      '        '
      
        '          '#39'Inhabits reef areas.  The parrotfish'#39'#39'#39's teeth are ' +
        'fused together,'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' enabling them to scrape away hard coral outer skelet' +
        'ons to get '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'at polyps inside.  These fish are thought to be a maj' +
        'or factor i'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'n reef recycling.'#39'#10#10'#39'Occasionally a female will c' +
        'hange sex, increa'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'se in size, and take on a distinct appearance  as a t' +
        'erminal-pha'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'se male.  This is usually done to replace a missing m' +
        'ale.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibi'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'lity is poor. '#39'#10#10'#39'Range is Bermuda and Florida to' +
        ' Brazil.'#39'#10#10'
