        '          '#39'Young barracuda live in inshore seagrass beds, while ' +
        'adults rang'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'e from inshore channels to the open ocean.  The barra' +
        'cuda feeds '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'on a wide variety of fishes.'#39'#10#10'#39'It frequently dri' +
        'fts just below th'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'e surface and is known to approach divers at very clo' +
        'se range.  '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'The long underslung jaw with its very sharp teeth can' +
        ' be disconc'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'erting.  Attacks on humans have reportedly been in cl' +
        'oudy water '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'when the victim is wearing bright diving gear or atte' +
        'mpting to s'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'pear the fish.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is good for small spe' +
        'cimens, but  larg'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'e barracuda can carry a fatal toxin.  There is no vis' +
        'ible way to'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' tell if the fish is harmful to eat.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is ' +
        'worldwide.'#39'#10'
