      '        26'
      '        '
      
        '          '#39'The French grunt drifts in large groups in sheltered ' +
        'reef areas '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'during the day.  It forages nearby for other fish at ' +
        'night.'#39'#10#10'#39'The'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' fish produces a grunt-like sound by grinding teeth l' +
        'ocated in t'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'he throat.  The sound is amplified by the adjacent sw' +
        'im bladder.'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'  During territorial skirmishes, male grunts will fac' +
        'e and push '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'each other with open mouths.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is exce' +
        'llent.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'Bermuda, South Carolina to Brazil, and the Gulf of Me' +
        'xico.'#39'#10'
