        '          '#39'Found in coral reefs, rocky flats, reef sand, and sea' +
        'grass habit'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ats.  This is one of the most successful "cleaner fis' +
        'h" in the t'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ropical West Atlantic.  It feeds on the parasites of ' +
        'other fish,'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' who come to the wrasse to be cleaned.'#39'#10#10'#39'Most bl' +
        'uehead wrasses ar'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'e yellow.  The head of the terminal-phase male (about' +
        ' 4% of the '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'population) is blue.'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is poor.'#39'#10#10' +
        #39'Range is large, includ'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ing both sides of the Atlantic, Bermuda, Bahamas, and' +
        ' Florida to'#39' +'
      '          '#39' Curacao, plus the Gulf of Mexico.'#39
