        '          '#39'Inhabits reef and mid-water areas, feeding on inverte' +
        'brates and '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'small fishes.  The adult is one of the few jacks with' +
        'out teeth.'#39'#10 +'
      
        '          #10'#39'The young fish seek out larger predators, such as ' +
        'sharks, for p'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'rotection.  Divers have reported young jacks wanting ' +
        'to join up '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'with them!'#39'#10#10'#39'Edibility is excellent.'#39'#10#10'#39'Rang' +
        'e is Indo-Pacific and S'#39' +'
      '          '#39'outhern California to Panama.'#39'#10'
