      '        '
      
        '          '#39'Schools are found over rocky bottoms and around kelp ' +
        'forest cano'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'pies.  Not a true bass, this is the largest of the cr' +
        'oakers on t'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'he Pacific Coast.  It feeds in mid-water on squid, an' +
        'chovies, an'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'd sardines.  '#39'#10#10'#39'Croakers make a remarkable "boop' +
        '-boop-boop" sound'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39', and submarine commanders discovered they could hide' +
        ' the sound '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'of their engines behind the racket.  '#39'#10#10'#39'The larg' +
        'e calcareous "ear'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'stones" in this fish'#39'#39'#39's inner ear canals were cons' +
        'idered good luc'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'k charms by early Europeans and were used by American' +
        ' Indians in'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' jewelry.'#39'#10#10'#39'Excellent edibility if you can find ' +
        'one.  White sea b'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ass were heavily fished in the 1950s but are now rare' +
        'ly caught.'#39'#10 +'
      '          #10'#39'Range is from Alaska to Southern Baja.'#39'#10'
