        '          '#39'Found almost everywhere by divers, this fish lives ei' +
        'ther in sch'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ools or alone.  It is a voracious eater that feeds co' +
        'nstantly.  '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'It is also a very successful "cleaner fish", and a si' +
        'ngle Senori'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'ta may be surrounded by dozens of fishes waiting to b' +
        'e cleaned o'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'f parasites.  Divers report them teaming up to clean ' +
        'a large sea'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39' bass or Mola.'#39'#10#10'#39'This fish does not reverse sex ' +
        'as most wrasses d'#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'o.  When disturbed, it burrows in the bottom sediment' +
        '.  It also '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'sleeps there with its head protruding from the sand.'#39 +
        '#10#10'#39'Edibility '#39' +'
      
        '          '#39'is poor.'#39'#10#10'#39'Range is Northern California to Centr' +
        'al Baja. '#39
